/// Checks what broken blocks drop (CAL-153) against what vanilla's own loot code gives for the
/// same blocks, tools, block entities and breakers: each block's table rolled from its random
/// sequence, made from the world's seed, with its conditions, bonuses, counts and copied
/// components; a shulker box's contents and name and a banner's patterns copied from their block
/// entities; a decorated pot's sherds, each a template, dropped as it cracks or kept on it; a
/// table another block's (a wall torch's, a torch's); and air's none. Then each sequence's next
/// draw, to show each was drawn from as many times as vanilla's. And where `popResource` puts what
/// a block drops, from the level's random, as java.util.Random(0) gives it, with nothing made but
/// the random drawn from where `block_drops` is off. The items and tables are read from the
/// vanilla data pack in the server jar at oracle/jars/, as the rig's adapter loads them, so it's
/// run from the repository's root. Then what enchanted swords' effects come to against mobs
/// (D438), enchanted armor's protection and immunity against damages (D439), and thorns'
/// effects on the attacker (D442). And a bow's enchantments on its arrows (CAL-159): power's damage
/// and punch's knockback for a hit an arrow dealt, not one its shooter dealt, and flame's ignite as
/// an arrow it shot is spawned. Then the arithmetic int providers (D523), as `ContextIntProvider`'s
/// own work them out, each input in turn, an overflow anywhere making the whole 0, as `getInt`
/// catches `getIntUnsafe`'s. Then looting's raise of a mob's equipment drop chances (D526).
module test.drops

import nbt.snbt.{parse}
import nbt.tag.{Tag}
import rig.registries.{load_vanilla}
import server.level.{Dropped, Level}
import world.chunk.{BlockStates}
import random.legacy.{LegacyRandom}
import random.taped.{TapedRandom}
import registry.components.{ItemCodecs}
import world.digging.{enchanted_value, value_effect}
import world.drops.{get_drops, loot_table_of}
import world.damage.{DamageTypes}
import world.living.{after_absorb, after_magic_absorb, armor_share}
import world.loot.{Attacked, Loot, LootEntity, LootParams, PostAttack, context_int, distance_holds, enchanted_amount, equipment_drop_chance, post_attack_effects, random_sequence, roll_table, spawned_effects, weapon_effects, worn_amount, worn_immune}
import world.random_sequences.{RandomSequences}
import worldgen.facts.{Facts}

